# REGRESSION (`todo/t0841`, R48 Track D1) — the `meta while` half of the same
# arm.
#
# `Stmt::MetaFor` and `Stmt::MetaWhile` share ONE match arm in
# `src/ir/lowering/liveness.rs`, so this cell and
# `cow_meta_for_zero_trip_body_kill.gg` sample the two SURFACE spellings that
# reach it. `meta while` is a compile-time GUARD (language-reference §19.28):
# with a false condition the body is emitted zero times, which is the same
# zero-trip shape the `meta for` cell builds with an empty range. Both are
# wired because the arm is the thing being pinned and either spelling could
# grow its own arm later.
#
# ⚠ THE FUNCTION IS DELIBERATELY NON-GENERIC. The first draft of this cell put
# the guard in `probe[T]` with `bitwidth(T) > 64`, and that spelling is GREEN at
# pre-fix HEAD — measured, rc 0, `ab` / `ab` on both lanes — as is a generic
# `meta for i in 0..0`. A generic body reaches the lowerer with its meta forms
# already resolved, so the walker never sees this arm there and the fixture
# would have been green before AND after: coverage in name only (Core #12).
# The non-generic spelling is the one that reproduces.
#
# AXIS CELL: loop kind = `meta while` · guard = FALSE (`1 > 2`, a plain
# function) · body = an ASSIGN-KILL of a name consumed above and read below ·
# name type = String (heap-forced).
#
# RED-VERIFIED at pre-fix HEAD, both lanes: `gg build` rc 101,
# `GIR validation errors: function @main: local _1 read after MoveZero in bb0`
# (C and `--backend=llvm`).

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    String s = mk("a", "b")
    Vector[String] v = []
    v.push(s)
    meta while 1 > 2:
        s = mk("c", "d")
    print(s)
    print(v[0])
